anging"},{"surface":"பிறவார்","parts":[{"text":"பிற","lemma":"பிற","gloss":"be born"},{"text":"ஆர்","lemma":"ஆர்","gloss":"negative third person plural suffix"}],"gloss":"they will not be born"},{"surface":"ஆயினும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"ஆயின்","gloss":"even if"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"concessive suffix"}],"gloss":"even if"},{"surface":"இமையத்து","parts":[{"text":"இமையத்து","lemma":"இமையத்து","gloss":"of the Himalayas"}],"gloss":"of the Himalayas","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கோடு","parts":[{"text":"கோடு","lemma":"கோடு","gloss":"peak"}],"gloss":"peak"},{"surface":"உயர்ந்தன்ன","parts":[{"text":"உயர்ந்தன்ன","lemma":"உயர்ந்தன்ன","gloss":"like the rising"}],"gloss":"like the rising","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தம்","parts":[{"text":"தம்","lemma":"தான்","gloss":"their"}],"gloss":"their"},{"surface":"இசை","parts":[{"text":"இசை","lemma":"இசை","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"fame"},{"surface":"நட்டு","parts":[{"text":"நட்டு","lemma":"நட்டு","gloss":"establishing"}],"gloss":"establishing","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தீது","parts":[{"text":"தீது","lemma":"தீது","gloss":"blemish/evil"}],"gloss":"blemish"},{"surface":"இல்","parts":[{"text":"இல்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without"},{"surface":"யாக்கையடு","parts":[{"text":"யாக்கையடு","lemma":"யாக்கையடு","gloss":"with the body"}],"gloss":"with the body","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மாய்தல்","parts":[{"text":"மாய்","lemma":"மாய்","gloss":"perish"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"தல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"perishing"},{"surface":"தவ","parts":[{"text":"தவ","lemma":"தவ","gloss":"exceedingly"}],"gloss":"exceedingly"},{"surface":"தலையே","parts":[{"text":"தலை","lemma":"தலை","gloss":"supreme/best"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"the best"}]}],"literal":"\"Shall we do good deeds?\" thinking thus, / those who do not clear their doubts, whose vision is filled with impurities, / who have no resolve in their persistent hearts, / a hunter of elephants may obtain an elephant, / a hunter of quails may return with empty hands, / therefore, for those who have risen with high aims, / if attaining the fruits of deeds done is true, / enjoyment in the uncreated world is also possible, / if enjoyment in the uncreated world is not there, / non-existence of rebirth after changing is also possible, / even if they are not born again, like the Himalayas / establishing their fame high as its peaks, / perishing with a blemishless body is exceedingly the best.","translation":"Those whose minds are clouded by doubts, whose vision is filled with impurities, and whose persistent hearts lack resolve, hesitate, wondering, 'Shall we do good deeds or not?' But look: a hunter who sets out to hunt an elephant may indeed capture an elephant, while a hunter who goes after a tiny quail may return empty-handed. Therefore, for those who strive with high and noble aims, if the fruits of their deeds are real, they will attain enjoyment in the next world. Even if there is no such enjoyment in that uncreated world, they may escape the cycle of rebirth altogether. And even if they do not escape rebirth, establishing a fame as high as the peaks of the Himalayas and dying with a blemishless body is, above all, the supreme achievement.","modern":"‘நாம் நல்வினைகளைச் செய்வோமா மாட்டோமா?’ என்று ஐயம் நீங்காத, அறியாமை நிறைந்த அறிவையும், உறுதியற்ற நெஞ்சத்தையும் உடையவர்கள் துணிவில்லாதவர்கள் ஆவர். யானையை வேட்டையாடச் செல்பவன் யானையைப் பெறவும் கூடும்; காடையை வேட்டையாடச் செல்பவன் வெறும் கையோடு திரும்பவும் கூடும். அதனால், உயர்ந்த குறிக்கோளைக் கொண்டு முயன்ற உயர்ந்தோர்க்கு, அவர்கள் செய்த நல்வினைகளின் பயனாக, மறுவுலகத்து இன்பம் கிடைப்பதும் கூடும். அப்படிப்பட்ட மறுவுலக இன்பம் இல்லை என்றாலும், பிறவிச் சுழற்சியிலிருந்து விடுபடுதல் கூடும். அவ்வாறு பிறவாமை கூடாவிட்டாலும், இமயமலையின் சிகரத்தைப் போலத் தம் புகழை நிலைநிறுத்தி, பழி இல்லாத உடம்போடு இறப்பது எல்லாவற்றிலும் மிகச் சிறந்ததாகும்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Potuviyal tiṇai and Poruṇmoḻik kāñci tuṟai, where the poet-king Kōpperuñ Cōḻaṉ offers profound counsel on life, action, and legacy. He addresses those who hesitate to perform noble deeds due to doubt and lack of resolve. Using the vivid contrast of an elephant hunter who succeeds and a quail hunter who fails, he illustrates that aiming high is always superior, regardless of the immediate outcome. He argues that high endeavors yield three noble possibilities: heavenly bliss, liberation from rebirth, or at the very least, an enduring, mountain-like fame left behind on earth. The key words include 'உயர்ந்த வேட்டம்' (high aim/endeavor), 'இசை' (fame), and 'தீதில் யாக்கை' (blemishless body/life).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.1],[1.1,1.6],[1.6,2.0],[2.0,2.0],[2.0,2.8],[2.8,3.7],[3.7,4.1],[4.1,5.0],[5.0,5.6],[5.6,6.04],[6.04,6.12],[6.2,7.1],[7.1,7.4],[7.4,7.6],[7.6,8.0],[8.0,9.3],[9.3,9.3],[9.3,10.2],[10.2,10.6],[10.6,11.6],[11.6,12.0],[12.0,12.2],[12.2,13.01],[13.07,13.4],[13.4,14.6],[14.6,15.0],[15.0,15.1],[15.1,15.5],[15.5,16.7],[16.7,16.8],[16.8,17.6],[17.6,17.8],[18.92,19.52],[19.52,19.62],[19.62,20.52],[20.52,20.92],[20.92,22.02],[22.02,22.22],[22.22,22.52],[22.52,23.02],[23.02,24.22],[24.22,24.42],[24.42,24.62],[24.62,25.52],[25.52,26.12],[26.12,26.42],[26.42,26.62],[26.62,26.82],[26.82,27.92],[27.92,28.02],[28.02,28.42],[28.42,28.92],[28.92,29.42]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,0.95],[1.1,1.5],[1.5,1.9],[1.9,3.42],[3.42,3.46],[3.46,3.5],[3.5,3.7],[3.7,4.7],[4.7,5.54],[5.54,5.9],[6.03,6.3],[6.3,7.1],[7.1,7.5],[7.5,7.7],[7.7,8.2],[8.2,9.5],[9.5,9.6],[9.6,10.6],[10.6,11.0],[11.0,12.0],[12.0,12.3],[12.3,12.5],[12.5,13.32],[13.38,13.8],[13.8,14.7],[14.7,15.3],[15.3,15.4],[15.4,15.8],[15.8,17.1],[17.1,17.1],[17.1,18.1],[18.1,18.3],[19.32,19.92],[19.92,20.02],[20.02,20.92],[20.92,21.32],[21.42,22.62],[22.62,22.82],[22.82,23.02],[23.02,23.62],[23.62,24.92],[24.92,25.12],[25.12,25.42],[25.42,26.52],[26.52,27.22],[27.22,27.62],[27.62,27.82],[27.82,28.12],[28.12